WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.810
You open a banking app to check your card.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.850
For a moment, the full
16-digit number slides in.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.650
Then it's redrawn.

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.150
Stars, stars, stars, and
just the last 4 digits.

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.470
The whole number is still in the app.

6
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.630
So how does the program
pick out just the end?

7
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.730
In this mission, you'll see that a
string is a sequence of characters,

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.150
and each character has
a position, its index.

9
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.870
You'll find a string's length:
how many characters it holds.

10
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.750
And you'll take a
substring: part of a string,

11
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.630
picked out by position.

12
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.840
Your mission: find out how an app shows
only the last 4 digits of your card number.
